# Covers: an uncaught throw on a DETACHED strand is reported, not
#         swallowed.  The chunk itself succeeds -- its value is the inline
#         arm's -- so the return code cannot carry the failure, and the
#         detached arm has no caller to return one to.  Core design
#         section 9 routes it through the diag callback and the error
#         channel both; the REPL installs a diag hook that frames it the
#         same way it frames its own errors.
#
# Without that hook the detached arm here throws and the session prints
# nothing but `2` -- the "errors vanish" shape, moved from the batch path
# to the detached one.
#
# Ordering: the diag fires while the scheduler is still pumping, which is
# inside the same urbi_run that later prints the chunk's value, so the
# `!!!` line comes first.
#
# `,` detaches the LEFT arm, so `{ throw 1 }` is the detached one and
# `{ Realm.b = 2 }` runs inline as the chunk's value.

var b = 0
{ throw 1 } , { Realm.b = 2 }
Realm.b
[00000000] 0
[00000000] !!! 1
[00000000] 2
[00000000] 2
